PART 0 - CONTEXT AND RULES
================================================================================

0.1 CONTEXT AND GOAL

iveo is a page builder: creators add blocks (links, support, platform cards, players, forms) to a public page at iveo.site/@username, styled with a "vibe", and manage it from a dashboard (Links, Appearance, Contacts, Analytics, Settings). Sign-in and accounts are handled by Clerk.

Two areas still feel messy:
1. The editors for platform blocks (LinkedIn, X, YouTube, GitHub, Spotify, Instagram, Facebook, Threads, Discord, Linktree, Pinterest ...). The LinkedIn editor opens inline in the list, is about two and a half phone screens tall, puts the preview at the bottom, shows platform-specific look names, and leaks owner-facing wording onto the public card.
2. The /account page, which stacks three custom cards on top of Clerk's own profile component rendered inline. It looks like another app pasted into iveo, and profile, passkeys and plan are each handled in more than one place.

GOAL
- One small, consistent editor for every platform block, with one set of card looks and a short list of styling options.
- Spotify and Pinterest supported safely (server-side secrets, caching, graceful fallbacks, brand rules).
- One iveo-native Account area where profile, sign-in security, connected platforms, plan and data each have exactly one home, and every Clerk screen that remains is themed as iveo.
- Nothing is removed, nothing breaks, and the result works on a 360px phone and a 1440px desktop.


