0.4 VOCABULARY (add to the master glossary)

- Card: a platform block drawn as a card on the public page. Profile card = a person, channel or organisation (avatar-led). Item card = a single thing such as a track, video or pin (artwork-led).
- Player: a playable or interactive embed (YouTube video, Spotify, SoundCloud, Pinterest widget, Instagram/Facebook/Threads post).
- Look: the visual style of a card (LK-1). Options: the small set of styling controls (LK-11).
- Provider: a platform iveo understands; a provider definition is one file (PV-1).
- Source: the link or connected account a card reads from. Snapshot: the stored copy of what the provider returned (PV-4).
- Connected platform: a third-party account the owner authorised with OAuth (managed only in Account > Connected platforms, AR-3).
- "Embed" means only the Share sheet's site widget.


0.5 SHARED DESIGN RULES (recap of the master prompt so this file stands alone)

- Tokens: spacing 4/8/12/16/24/32/48; corners Sharp 6px, Rounded 16px, Pill 999px (large surfaces cap Pill at 28px); control radius 12px; 1px neutral borders; shadows only on floating layers.
- Buttons: four types only - Primary (solid dark), Secondary (outlined), Tertiary (text), Destructive (red, only for destructive actions); 44px high on touch; one primary per section or view; never a primary action as grey text.
- Choice controls: segmented control for 2-4 short options; tile grid for visual options; select for long lists; switches (never checkboxes) for on/off. Selected = filled dark (segments, chips) or dark ring plus check (tiles); unselected = outline or plain; disabled = 50% opacity with a reason.
- Sections: H2 + one-line description + one flat card with divider rows; accordions (one open at a time, header shows the current value) for secondary groups; never nested tabs.
- Forms: label above, white inputs with a 1px border, 44px high, inline validation, counters where limits exist. Instant choices autosave and show "Saved"; text forms use an explicit Save in the section footer, disabled until dirty.
- Badges: PRO (only for users who lack access), status chip (dot + text), type badge (neutral).
- Copy: sentence case, buttons start with a verb, helper text at most about 90 characters, no marketing, brand "iveo" always lower case, no vendor names in iveo-owned text.
- Accessibility: 44px targets, text contrast 4.5:1 and component borders 3:1, keyboard path for everything (including drag and drop), visible focus ring, reduced motion, safe areas, dialogs and sheets trap focus.
- Public page: two shells (BUTTON shell for simple links, SURFACE shell for rich blocks), tokens --surface, --border, --text, --text-muted, --button-*, --accent, corners token; vibes change paint, not structure.


