PV-8 SPOTIFY (checked against Spotify's documentation in November 2026; re-check before coding, RU-10).
- Kinds: track, album, playlist, artist, show, episode. Accept open.spotify.com links (with or without an intl- path), spotify: URIs and spotify.link short links; strip ?si= and utm parameters.
- Player, no credentials needed: an iframe to https://open.spotify.com/embed/{kind}/{id}?utm_source=generator, width 100%, no border, lazy, allow="autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; fullscreen; picture-in-picture", title "{Title} on Spotify", corners from the Corners token. Sizes follow Spotify's "Choosing an Embed size" guide (typically about 152px compact and 352px standard). Display as defaults to Player. Spotify's Embeds Terms of Use apply.
- Card metadata: the Web API with the client-credentials flow, server-side only. POST https://accounts.spotify.com/api/token with grant_type=client_credentials and the id and secret from SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID and SPOTIFY_CLIENT_SECRET; cache the token for its lifetime minus 60 seconds; allow one refresh in flight at a time; refresh once on a 401. Fetch one item per request (GET /v1/tracks/{id}, /albums/{id}, /artists/{id}, /playlists/{id}, /shows/{id}, /episodes/{id}); the batch endpoints were removed.
- What changed in 2026 and must be tolerated: Development Mode apps need the app owner to hold an active Spotify Premium subscription (if it lapses the API stops working); new apps are limited in the number of client IDs per developer and to 5 authorised users (this affects user sign-in flows, not catalogue reads); fields were removed (artist followers and popularity, track and album popularity, show publisher, available markets); playlist contents only come back for playlists the user owns or collaborates on; search returns at most 10 results. So: never rely on removed fields; Spotify cards have no "Show stats" (hide the toggle); show playlist metadata only (name, description, cover, owner name if present), never a track list.
- Failure order: Web API -> oEmbed (https://open.spotify.com/oembed?url=..., no credentials, gives title and thumbnail) -> manual details. On a 429 honour Retry-After and serve the snapshot. If every Web API call starts failing (for example the owner's Premium lapsed) switch the whole provider to oEmbed and log an alert; visitors never see an error.
- Brand and display rules (Spotify Design & Branding Guidelines): any card showing Spotify metadata or artwork carries the Spotify logo - the full logo (icon plus wordmark) at least 70px wide, or the icon alone (at least 21px) only when space is short; the green logo only on black or white backgrounds, otherwise a monochrome logo (black on light, white on dark); keep the logo's clear space (half the icon height); never put it on artwork or a busy area; never pair it with another brand in one lock-up. Artwork stays unmodified: no cropping, blur, tint, overlay or animation, no text or controls on top of it, corners rounded at 4px (8px on large screens). Titles and names appear exactly as Spotify provides them and may be truncated only if the full text stays reachable (title attribute and accessible name). Every card links back to Spotify with "Listen on Spotify" (or "Play on Spotify" / "Open Spotify") in a new tab. Lay out for names of about 25 characters (playlist, album), 18 (artist) and 23 (track).
- Looks for Spotify: the artwork sits in its own opaque square slot in every look; Banner uses a solid or gradient banner, never the artwork; Compact uses a 48px square artwork. Spotify green is used only for the button or glyph accent, with black text on it.
- Terms: Spotify's Developer Terms and Developer Policy apply, including the limits on using Spotify content to train machine-learning models and on building streaming services. Store only what the card needs; refresh at least daily and drop snapshots of deleted items.

PV-9 PINTEREST (checked in November 2026; re-check before coding, RU-10).
- Kinds: pin, board, profile. Accept pinterest.com and pin.it links.
- Public content needs no credentials. Players use Pinterest's official widgets: a plain anchor with data-pin-do="embedPin", "embedBoard" or "embedUser" plus the single pinit.js script (//assets.pinterest.com/js/pinit.js, async defer), loaded once per page, only when a Pinterest player is on that page, and ideally after the visitor scrolls it into view or taps it. Widgets are shown unmodified (no overlays or restyling) and sized by the Size control. Display as defaults to Player.
- API access: the owner's app id and access token (PINTEREST_APP_ID, PINTEREST_ACCESS_TOKEN) belong to the owner's own Pinterest developer app and account. Use them only for the owner's own content during development (for example a test "Connect Pinterest" flow); never use them to fetch other creators' content or to serve visitors. API v5 facts that shape this: apps with Trial access get 1,000 requests per day and calls can fail with a 401 ("consumer type is not supported") until Trial access is approved; the app secret is unavailable while Trial is pending; pins created under Trial are sandbox-only; Standard access (a review with a demo video of the OAuth flow) allows 100 requests per second per user per app and is needed for real creators.
- Per-creator connection (optional, behind PINTEREST_OAUTH_ENABLED, off until Standard access is granted): the OAuth authorization-code flow with read-only scopes (boards:read, pins:read, user_accounts:read), client secret from PINTEREST_APP_SECRET, tokens encrypted at rest, refresh handled on the server, listed and revoked in Account > Connected platforms. It enables Card display (cover, title, board name, pin count) for the creator's own boards and pins. Until it exists, Pinterest Card display uses manual details (ED-13) and the widget is the default.
- Brand: use Pinterest's widgets and buttons as provided, always link back, never alter pins. Pinterest red is only the button or glyph accent (contrast guard).

PV-10 PRIVACY AND THIRD-PARTY SCRIPTS. Players load third-party iframes or scripts only when needed: lazy, and behind a click-to-load facade (poster plus play glyph, same size) wherever that does not change how playback works today; never on first paint (master PG-38); referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin"; one script per provider per page (Pinterest: once); no provider tracking before interaction. Cards (images and text) need no provider script at all.

PV-11 ANALYTICS. A click on a card or player's button counts as a link click exactly like any link today (block id, the same events, GA4 and Meta Pixel unchanged). Do not add provider SDKs to measure plays.

PV-12 LIMITS, ABUSE, MONITORING. Rate-limit the resolve endpoint per user (for example 20 per minute). Cache resolved public data by canonical URL for all users (6-24 hours per provider) so repeated blocks do not multiply API calls. Log provider status codes and latency without secrets. Alert when a provider fails more than 20% of calls over 15 minutes, or when a required secret is missing in production.


